; Settings for the 2ksbox OpenGL pass-through (OPENGL32.DLL). Put this
; file in the folder the game's EXE is in.
;
;   ExtensionsYear,N    hide OpenGL extensions newer than year N
;   GL_EXT_name         hide that one extension
;   +GL_EXT_name        show it again (only with ExtensionsYear set)
;
; The year is set because a modern host reports several thousand
; characters of extension names, and games of the 1990s read that into a
; fixed buffer. GLQuake's is 4096 bytes: given the whole string it dies
; with an invalid page fault in an unknown module, having returned into
; the text of the extension list itself.
;
; Raise the year for a later game, or delete the file to pass everything
; through. SETUP /GAME never overwrites a copy that is already there.

ExtensionsYear,1997
